  ("Robert Dicke was working on how to find the very thing they were trying so diligently to get" 0.11909 0.88138 0.52773 0.5435 0.5435 0.01578 0.00504 0.3048 0.0550 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("rid of. The Princeton researchers were pursuing an idea that had been suggested in the 1940s" 0.11909 0.88145 0.54412 0.55989 0.55989 0.01578 0.00504 0.2334 0.0224 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("by the Russian-born astrophysicist George Gamow that if you looked deep enough into space" 0.11909 0.88145 0.56051 0.57628 0.57628 0.01578 0.00504 0.2729 0.0202 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("you should find some cosmic background radiation left over from the Big Bang. Gamow" 0.11909 0.88149 0.5769 0.59267 0.59267 0.01578 0.00504 0.2608 0.0303 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("calculated that by the time it crossed the vastness of the cosmos, the radiation would reach" 0.11909 0.88147 0.59329 0.60906 0.60906 0.01578 0.00504 0.2496 0.0818 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("Earth in the form of microwaves. In a more recent paper he had even suggested an instrument" 0.11909 0.88147 0.60967 0.62545 0.62545 0.01578 0.00504 0.3024 0.0437 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("that might do the job: the Bell antenna at Holmdel. Unfortunately, neither Penzias and" 0.11909 0.88147 0.62606 0.64184 0.64184 0.01578 0.00504 0.2700 0.0303 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("Wilson, nor any of the Princeton team, had read Gamow’s paper." 0.11909 0.64369 0.64253 0.6583 0.6583 0.01578 0.00504 0.3553 0.0632 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("The noise that Penzias and Wilson were hearing was, of course, the noise that Gamow had" 0.13924 0.8816 0.67552 0.69129 0.69129 0.01578 0.00504 0.3239 0.0314 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("postulated. They had found the edge of the universe, or at least the visible part of it, 90 billion" 0.11909 0.88139 0.69191 0.70768 0.70768 0.01578 0.00504 0.2736 0.0879 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("trillion miles away. They were “seeing” the first photons—the most ancient light in the" 0.11909 0.88156 0.7083 0.72407 0.72407 0.01578 0.00504 0.2975 0.0550 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("universe—though time and distance had converted them to microwaves, just as Gamow had" 0.11909 0.88156 0.72461 0.74039 0.74039 0.01578 0.00504 0.3103 0.1446 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  (#("predicted. In his book The Inflationary Universe , Alan Guth provides an analogy that helps to" 23 49 (pdf-text-emph italic)) 0.11909 0.88155 0.741 0.75678 0.75678 0.01578 0.00504 0.2935 0.0802 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("put this finding in perspective. If you think of peering into the depths of the universe as like" 0.11909 0.88156 0.75739 0.77317 0.77317 0.01578 0.00504 0.2343 0.0258 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("looking down from the hundredth floor of the Empire State Building (with the hundredth floor" 0.11909 0.88133 0.77378 0.78956 0.78956 0.01578 0.00504 0.3208 0.0617 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("representing now and street level representing the moment of the Big Bang), at the time of" 0.11909 0.88149 0.79017 0.80595 0.80595 0.01578 0.00504 0.2767 0.0997 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("Wilson and Penzias’s discovery the most distant galaxies anyone had ever detected were on" 0.11909 0.88143 0.80656 0.82234 0.82234 0.01578 0.00504 0.2585 0.0581 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("about the sixtieth floor, and the most distant things—quasars—were on about the twentieth." 0.11909 0.88149 0.82295 0.83873 0.83873 0.01578 0.00504 0.3297 0.0448 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("Penzias and Wilson’s finding pushed our acquaintance with the visible universe to within half" 0.11909 0.88159 0.83934 0.85512 0.85512 0.01578 0.00504 0.3002 0.0617 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("an inch of the sidewalk." 0.11909 0.31133 0.8558 0.87158 0.87158 0.01578 0.00504 0.3084 0.0190 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("Still unaware of what caused the noise, Wilson and Penzias phoned Dicke at Princeton and" 0.13924 0.88142 0.8888 0.90457 0.90457 0.01578 0.00504 0.3094 0.0337 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("described their problem to him in the hope that he might suggest a solution. Dicke realized at" 0.11909 0.88155 0.90518 0.92096 0.92096 0.01578 0.00504 0.3005 0.0774 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
