  ("which point, presumably, you would rather lose heart in the exercise and give up). The reason" 0.11909 0.88155 0.82367 0.83944 0.83944 0.01578 0.00504 0.2875 0.0493 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("for this is that the universe bends, in a way we can’t adequately imagine, in conformance with" 0.11909 0.88148 0.84005 0.85583 0.85583 0.01578 0.00504 0.3123 0.0235 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("Einstein’s theory of relativity (which we will get to in due course). For the moment it is" 0.11909 0.88149 0.85644 0.87222 0.87222 0.01578 0.00504 0.2786 0.0807 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("enough to know that we are not adrift in some large, ever-expanding bubble. Rather, space" 0.11909 0.88155 0.87283 0.88861 0.88861 0.01578 0.00504 0.2463 0.0594 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
  ("curves, in a way that allows it to be boundless but finite. Space cannot even properly be said" 0.11909 0.88165 0.88922 0.905 0.905 0.01578 0.00504 0.2570 0.0577 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" 0.0143 nil nil 0 "KOPLLM+TimesNewRoman" nil)
